      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5aab30ea0b6da707273dbb98|full_name}: Well, it still surprise old menu can remember the position. So why can it not just done for new menu.\nI hope developers can find the trick to skip a part faster. Because right now it's just not great at all, if you think every day like 20 or more worlds are added, in Community Labs and New. That is a lot. Scrolling again down is no fun at all. Remember where it was scrolled will a big plus for explorers!\nSome people hates this way already and give up on exploring new worlds and stick just on some known good worlds. That is it. Even good worlds will forgotten very fast.",
